medaled at a World Cup event. Brassard placed seventh in the qualifying. In the final, Lahtela and Mustonen again surprised, placing 1-2 until Moseley made his run. But Moseley won the gold medal comfortably. He had the fastest run of the final and the highest point score, using his signature “helicopter cross,” a 360° twist with crossed skis. Lahtela would return in 2002 to win the gold medal. He competed at every Olympic moguls competition thru 2006. Moseley would also return in 2002 and placed fourth at Salt Lake. Brassard placed fourth in Nagano, hurt by his air points score."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/99771"} "Jonny Moseley"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "26.53 (1)"] [:td {} "26.93 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88817"} "Janne Lahtela"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "25.43 (2)"] [:td {} "26.00 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/99772"} "Sami Mustonen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "25.16 (3)"] [:td {} "25.76 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:t